                <pb facs="0751" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg669"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Chargé d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The National Assembly may wish, if possible, to continue in session until the
                    arrival at Managua of the currency experts, collector general of customs, and
                    assistants, who will start before December 1. The assembly may wish to decide
                    after their arrival whether they need further legislation to carry out the
                    projected financial reforms.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
